WEBVTT

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:11.510
Toki!

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.910
Hey.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.040
Ryuuka, Sera...

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:00.180
<b>Round 9:
Best</b>

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.000
East Hand 1

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.000
Dealer: Miyanaga Teru

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.250
South Player

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.250
Hanada Kirame

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.750
West Player

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.750
Matsumi Kuro

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.960
North Player

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.960
Onjouji Toki

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.760
<i>The dora are coming in nicely.</i>

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.060
<i>In the second round match,</i>

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.600
<i>I lost the points that gave 
Onjouji-san a 90,000 point lead.</i>

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:27.900
<i>Today, there's someone even scarier.</i>

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.810
<i>But still... this time...</i>

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.910
<i>I can't lose!</i>

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:37.870
Riichi.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:47.200
Senriyama's Onjouji attacks 
first with a riichi!

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.080
<i>Marvelous!</i>

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.300
Tsumo. 2,000. 4,000.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.260
<i>Marvelous!</i>

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.290
<i>Onjouji-san... she really is strong.</i>

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.350
<i>I felt like there was 
something behind me.</i>

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:32.840
<i>Did I imagine it?</i>

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.660
<i>That feeling just now...</i>

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.920
<i>I wonder if that's what 
Sera talked about.</i>

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.030
<i>Has she seen through me already?</i>

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:48.140
<i>Let's see what the 
inter-high champion's got.</i>

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.940
The first strike is an ippatsu!

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:53.190
By Senriyama's Onjouji Toki!

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.510
Starting at the regional matches,

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.860
and now at this tournament,

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.690
she's had quite a few ippatsu wins.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:06.450
First Players' Match, First Half - East Hand 1 East Player
Shiraitodai High School (West Tokyo)
3rd year Miyanaga Teru

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.110
The champion Miyanaga Teru

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.620
has suddenly dropped to last place

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.910
because of the dealer penalty!

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.760
I feel like it's a bit of a waste when

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.450
Miyanaga is the starting dealer.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.360
Oh? What do you mean by that?

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:13.670
Miyanaga often doesn't 
win in East Hand 1,

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.880
but this is quite well-known...

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.970
Oh, isn't that really risky though?

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.010
In team tournaments, she only 
does it in the first half.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:26.590
Apparently, she uses that one 
hand to observe her opponents.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:29.020
Like habits and discard strategies?

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.510
No, according to pro players 
who have played her,

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:36.310
it's more like she sees through 
you to your core...

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.440
Like a magical mirror that 
shows one's true self.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.320
Magical mirror? Say what?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.820
East Hand 2

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.820
Dealer: Hanada Kirame

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.160
<i>I feel like the champion</i>

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:50.040
<i>looked at something that's 
important to me...</i>

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:55.580
Ron.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.500
1,000.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:05:59.960
Y-Yes!

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:03.030
The winner of the second 
hand is Miyanaga Teru!

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:04.690
Is the champion's single-handed

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.720
domination about to start again?

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.510
Inter-high champion?

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.100
Yeah, she's not to be trifled with.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.400
What's going on?

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.410
Whoa, the Weekly Mahjong Today!

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.610
I borrowed the second copy 
from Adamine's club room.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.250
Nice.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:30.490
I know her! Miyanaga Teru!

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.930
From Shiraitodai.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:34.110
She facilitated their 
two year winning streak.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:37.500
Maybe we'll see her with our own eyeballs,
 if we make it to the tournament.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.890
Eyeballs?

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.460
What's scary about her is this:

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.500
Her winning hand streak.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.870
What's more, every successive 
winning hand is worth more.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.370
I wouldn't want to face her.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.580
She sounds scary.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.270
<i>Right now, I'm...</i>

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.480
<i>Facing off against that champion!</i>

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.940
East Hand 3 - 6th turn

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.000
Dealer: Matsumi Kuro

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.700
<i>I'm not going to let you 
get your winning streak.</i>

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.160
Riichi!

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:19.460
<i>Riichi after discarding 
the tile she drew!</i>

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.830
<i>Is this going to be another ippatsu?</i>

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.780
<i>Marvelous, I didn't have any 
safe tiles, but she saved me.</i>

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:30.570
<i>Following her lead!</i>

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.060
Pon.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:35.430
<i>She called the tile she 
just discarded herself?!</i>

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.460
A pon from the champion!

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.880
She just called the tile she discarded!

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.930
What could this mean?

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:45.440
I think she did it to stop Onjouji's ippatsu,

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.400
but I can't say if it was on purpose.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.860
<i>If Onjouji-san was expecting 
an ippatsu tsumo,</i>

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:55.820
<i>then this is her winning tile...</i>

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.130
Ron.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:11.530
1,300.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.020
Yes.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:19.020
<i>This is the first time we've met,</i>

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:21.020
<i>but she's already completely 
seen through me.</i>

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.980
East Hand 4

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:30.160
Tsumo.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.780
1,000. 2,000.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.230
Miyanaga Teru strikes again!

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:39.160
Has her winning streak begun after all?!

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.070
Uhh, one, two...

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.840
It's three wins in a row!

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.690
Plus, the hands are worth more every time.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:48.420
It's just like in the magazine!

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.220
Toki...

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.970
South Hand 1

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.220
We're in South Hand 1 now and 
the champion is dealer again!

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.950
This time, she won't be observing!

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:05.130
<i>I won't stand a chance if she 
keeps winning as the dealer.</i>

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:07.350
<i>So let's stop her quickly.</i>

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.480
Riichi!

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.060
Ron.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:09.860
Marvelous?

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.530
7,700.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.990
Four in a row!

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:26.080
South Hand 1, Bonus 1

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:55.390
<i>Miyanaga will tsumo a dealer mangan 
with the 6 of bamboo in the next turn.</i>

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:56.570
<i>I won't let her!</i>

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:57.610
Pon!

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:03.790
<i>I disrupted the order and 
I know what she needs.</i>

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:04.700
Tsumo.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.460
4,100 all.

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:11.460
Tsumo for a dealer mangan!

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.330
<i>She won despite the disruption?</i>

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:17.240
<i>And this makes it five in a row!</i>

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:19.640
<i>Is she just going to end it by herself?!</i>

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.010
That was...

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:24.330
Yeah, a call that doesn't 
advance her hand.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:25.840
I'm sure it was...

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:26.930
But!

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:30.440
Are you saying Miyanaga Teru 
surpasses Toki's predictions?

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:32.940
I guess so.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.200
Toki...

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:46.410
South Hand 1, Bonus 2

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:46.410
Dealer: Miyanaga Teru

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:57.840
<i>She's going to get 6,000 
from all in one turn?!</i>

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:10.640
<i>I can't even disrupt it.</i>

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.660
Tsumo, 6,200 all.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:38.670
<i>Tsumo! 6,200 all! Six wins in a row!</i>

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.680
<i>And it's a dealer haneman!</i>

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:43.570
<i>Nobody can stop her now!</i>

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:47.600
This is the pinnacle 
of high school players!

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.170
Miyanaga Teru!

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.210
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:58.560
<i>She goes beyond what I imagined.</i>

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:00.650
<i>Guys...</i>

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.560
Shiraitodai played with a different 
order in the spring tournament,

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.950
so Toki didn't get to 
play against Miyanaga.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:10.860
Yeah.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.460
It's really rough that 
this is her first match.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.300
Toki...

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:37.830
Toki!

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:40.150
Hey.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:46.470
Ryuuka, Sera.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.270
I'm sorry I was late today.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:51.580
It's fine, I saw your email.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.590
The nurse messed up

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.400
and the examination took longer.

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.250
Wait, why are you both here?

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.320
Did the club finish meeting already?

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:02.410
Today the starting members

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:04.130
for the fall preliminaries 
were announced.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.820
Oh, and what about me?

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:08.950
You're the ace.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:12.980
Seriously? But you're the ace, Sera.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.280
Our coach made the decision based 
on your recent performance.

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:18.880
That's right, you should 
be more confident.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.150
Yup, yup.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:24.180
What? You're not happy?

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:28.160
I am... but I'm feeling the pressure,

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:29.660
and I feel bad for you.

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:30.850
You idiot!

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:32.870
It's actually worse to have

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.120
you be like that when I don't care at all.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.230
I care more about the 
fact that the team's

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:39.420
getting stronger than my position.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.770
Last year we were defeated,

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:44.230
but next year, I want us to 
win against Shiraitodai.

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:45.300
Yeah.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:48.890
So you're planning on pitting 
me against that monster.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.690
It'll be fine.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:56.230
You'll just have to get even better.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:01.730
I'm sorry.

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.860
I might not be able to live 
up to your expectations.

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:07.380
Why not?

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.620
You're a lot stronger now than 
before you were hospitalized.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.920
To be honest, my actual skill

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.620
is the same as when I was on the 3rd team.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:17.050
Meaning?

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.170
You won't believe it,

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:24.060
but when I collapsed, 
I teetered between life and death.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:26.130
After I came back, I started seeing it.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.890
One turn ahead...

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:37.760
For real?

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:41.340
Remember how FunaQ said that my style

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.230
changed since I was discharged?

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:46.880
Almost as if I "can see one turn ahead"?

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:50.410
That was actually spot on.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.510
That's amazing!

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:57.270
So that's how you got your 
riichi ippatsu percentage!

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.170
If nobody called a tile, you hit 
it nearly 100% of the time!

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:01.920
And when someone called,

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.310
the tile that should have been yours 
was always your winning tile!

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:06.740
I always thought it was strange.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:09.250
You're undefeatable, if 
you can really do that!

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:12.380
B-But... if I react to what I've seen

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:14.470
and change my actions,

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.600
I can't see anything 
for about two turns...

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:21.680
So? That's still amazing, right, Ryuuka?

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:26.320
Toki...

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:29.780
Ryuuka?

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:33.240
We might be able to win...

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:35.580
against Shiraitodai!

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:01.020
<i>I'm sorry, guys.</i>

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.150
Chi!

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:07.370
<i>After all this, I'm still just 
the girl from the 3rd team</i>

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:09.290
<i>who adored you two.</i>

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:10.650
Pon!

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:17.470
<i>This person from Fukuoka got wrecked</i>

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.750
<i>by Miyanaga Teru in the second round match,</i>

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.990
<i>but she's still trying to attack...</i>

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.210
<b>Marvelous!</b>

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:30.320
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.010
<i>Toki, that won't pass.</i>

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:34.340
Ron!

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:39.980
Oh man, I've been overtaken.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.390
Toki, your draws are as weak as always.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.710
No no, she just declares riichi too easily.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:47.860
Really?

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:50.610
You should have stayed silent.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:53.100
And declaring riichi now after

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:55.150
discarding this two turns ago is a bad idea.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:58.450
That's why you'll always 
be in the 3rd team.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:02.010
Ryuuka, you're always so harsh.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.580
On to the next game!

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:06.030
You don't mind playing me again?

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:08.950
Of course not. 
This is your training.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:10.670
Training, training!

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:14.690
Let's go again!

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:17.140
We won't go easy on you again!

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:21.730
<i>In the past, even if 
I couldn't win at all,</i>

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:25.350
<i>I really liked and enjoyed 
simply touching the tiles...</i>

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.950
<i>My responsibility and 
goals are a heavy burden,</i>

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:36.490
<i>but I want to at least play</i>

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.030
<i>like I used to back then, again.</i>

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:40.560
I'll pon that!

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:45.540
<i>Achiga gets all the dora, so it's easy 
to calculate what the hand's worth.</i>

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.420
<i>If she plays like that,</i>

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:49.620
<i>everybody knows that her hand is cheap.</i>

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:53.630
<i>I get it! She's doing it on purpose!</i>

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:10.320
<i>I won't deal into her hand with this.</i>

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:13.280
<i>Then maybe this?</i>

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:16.360
Ron!

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:19.620
1,000 in the third bonus hand is 1,900!

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.710
Shindouji's Hanada Kirame has put an end

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:25.620
to the champion's consecutive dealer streak!

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:28.700
<i>Can you hear the euphoria in the hall?!</i>

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:31.780
<i>This is the reaction to 
that tiny 1,000 point win!</i>

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:35.840
<i>Our audience watching the 
semifinals knows very well</i>

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:40.140
<i>how difficult it is to stop 
Miyanaga's winning streak.</i>

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:43.480
It looks like you finally realized.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:44.640
Marvelous.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:48.890
This table is not here just for you two.

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:54.870
<i>I see. It's obvious, but I forgot...</i>

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:59.240
<i>If I take the other players into account,</i>

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.410
<i>I can stop Miyanaga Teru!</i>

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.410
<i>I can still fight!</i>

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:06.700
That look on Onjouji-senpai's face...

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.430
Rather than her look,

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:10.670
her choice of discard in that hand

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.210
eliminates all doubt.

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:15.060
<i>It's quite obvious that Onjouji</i>

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:17.210
<i>purposely dealt into Hanada's hand.</i>

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:18.770
Ryuuka...

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:22.470
Yeah... Toki...

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:29.160
Hanada won...

